        quickSort.sort(array);
        assertArrayEquals(expected, array);
        System.out.println("Array with identical elements number of comparisons: " + quickSort.getComparisonCount());
    }
}
```

In this implementation, the `QuickSort` class can sort any array of comparable elements. The `comparisonCount` field tracks the number of comparisons made during sorting. The unit tests cover various edge cases:

1. Sorting an array of integers.
2. Sorting an array of strings.
3. Sorting an already sorted array.
4. Sorting a reverse sorted array.
5. Sorting an array with all identical elements.

